**SOLVED — the mic now works from the voice worker.** Final b68 probe: `caps 42  lastret 16000`, `mic stage 33 (done)`, `lasterr 0`, `mic fail none recorded`, `ready 1`. Captures complete in 1230 ms each and repeat every ~1230–1290 ms. One session (`open0 pid 4 seq 1`), no teardown, no wedge.

**SOLVED — the model and thresholds were never the problem.** `velapaw kws mic 1` on b68 returned `heard eight (0.941)` with peak 8202, rms 1344, profile `51 53 111 8046 8202 1443 3170 379`. In the dialog the worker read `eight 0.957`, `six 0.750`, `eight 0.445`. Against b62's 0.441/0.176/0.316 for the same word, this is a different regime — the weak scores were capture quality, not the classifier.

**RULED OUT — the GDMA descriptor-alignment theory.** Refuted because (a) captures have repeatedly succeeded on the same descriptors, including 16000 clean samples 20 s before a failure in the same boot; (b) our own `eofnum=0x0ffc` = 4092 B is the number all of mic.c's arithmetic is built on, so EOF demonstrably fires; (c) "Patch #16" is misattributed — it clears `I2S_TX_STOP_EN` (mic.h:41-43), not descriptor chains; (d) `lastret -999` is my sentinel for "the call never returned," not "the loop never completed a cycle"; (e) `caps 1` means one capture attempt, not repeated session opens; (f) 0x3fcbb2d0 − 0x3fcbb280 = 80 bytes, not a multiple of the 12-byte ESP32-S3 GDMA descriptor.

**NEWLY REPRODUCIBLE — the `-110` reopen bug.** Capture once from the CLI, then let the worker capture: `rec 0/18  play 1/1  phase -1  got 0/32000`. Head 18 means all buffers reached es8311's pendq; tail 0 means none came back. This has been an open backlog item with no repro since mic bring-up.

